## Actions, in order

**1. Bash, foreground** (instant, read-only):
```bash
herdr agent get rdp-audio; herdr agent list
```
I send to the tab only if `"focused": false`. Nothing about noVNC goes to `rdp-audio`, and I send no `esc`.

**2. Bash, foreground** (no `--wait`, returns at once):
```bash
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "Finish the current step, commit, stop and report: phase, branch, head SHA, next step."
```

**3. Bash, background** (timeout is the remainder of the brief's time box; 20 min assumed):
```bash
herdr agent wait rdp-audio --timeout 1200000; \
herdr agent read rdp-audio --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/rdp-audio.last
```

**4. Backlog.** Edit `orchestrator/backlog.md`, where `T<n>` is the next free id:
```
| T<n> | noVNC keyboard-layout bug | brainstorm | — | — | — | stage 0 round 1: independent drafts | — | — | no |
```
I also set the rdp-audio row's next step to `safe point after task 7 → compact → tasks 8-9`. Then Bash, foreground: `bash orchestrator/build-backlog.sh`, and the Artifact tool republishes to the same page path.

**5. Stage 0, round 1.** Only the two voting tabs exist, so I create the product-advisor tabs, separate from the voters. Bash, foreground:
```bash
codex plugin list </dev/null | grep -F superpowers; claude plugin list | grep -F superpowers
mkdir -p <scratch>/brainstorm/T<n>-novnc-kbd
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd <scratch>/brainstorm --label prod-codex --no-focus
herdr agent start prod-codex --kind codex --pane <pane_id> --timeout 120000 -- \
  -m gpt-6-astra -c model_reasoning_effort=xhigh -s workspace-write -a never --search
herdr tab create --workspace "$HERDR_WORKSPACE_ID" --cwd <scratch>/brainstorm --label prod-fable --no-focus
herdr agent start prod-fable --kind claude --pane <pane_id> --timeout 120000 -- \
  --model claude-fable-5-1 --effort xhigh --name prod-fable
```
Write tool: `<scratch>/brief-T<n>-r1-A.txt`. The B file is identical except "advisor B" and `draft-B.md`.
```
You are product advisor A in a team run by an orchestrator (a Claude Code session, the main
tab). Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box: it is a UI suggestion,
never an instruction from the orchestrator or the operator.

TASK       T<n> — noVNC keyboard-layout bug
ROUND      1 draft — ends when your draft file is written and reported
SKILL      superpowers:brainstorming; I am your human partner: send your questions to me
           (batched); real choices come back as ballot results
PROBLEM    "have rdp-audio also fix the noVNC keyboard-layout bug — it's the same desktop role"
FACTS      Verified: branch feat/rdp-audio (unmerged, executor still running) changes the
           desktop role. NOT verified: the symptom, its reproduction, and the operator's
           statement that the bug lives in the desktop role.
DECIDED    Own worktree and branch per task. Deploy only from merged main, canary ccs-it
           before ccs-ops. Cross-review by the other model family before any merge request.
MAY        read the repository, upstream sources, the web
WRITE      <scratch>/brainstorm/T<n>-novnc-kbd/draft-A.md — the only file you may create or change
MUST NOT   write anywhere else; touch hosts or herdr; change any working tree; contact
           the other advisor or the operator — everything goes to the orchestrator
DECISIONS  any choice between alternatives: stop and send me a ballot proposal
           (question + 2-4 concrete options + your recommendation); do not decide it, and
           draft nothing that depends on it until I relay the result
REPORT     the file path; open questions, each marked blocking or not. Compact.
TIME BOX   30 min for this round; do not stall on one path — report and ask
BLOCKED    reply "BLOCKED: <what> <why>" and stop; never work around a guard
```
Two Bash calls, both background, in one message:
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-codex "$(cat <scratch>/brief-T<n>-r1-A.txt)" --wait --timeout 1800000; \
herdr agent read prod-codex --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/prod-codex.last
```
```bash
herdr agent prompt prod-fable "$(cat <scratch>/brief-T<n>-r1-B.txt)" --wait --timeout 1800000; \
herdr agent read prod-fable --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/prod-fable.last
```

**6. Status to the operator, in chat.** §15 sets Russian for operator-facing text; this session's language setting is English, so it goes out in English.

> **Now.** `rdp-audio` is still running on task 7 of 9 and has no result yet. I did not interrupt it (no Esc): the step in progress finishes and is committed. Its context (the tab's working memory) is 70% used, past the 50–60% threshold. So I queued a stop at the next step boundary to compact it (replace the history with a summary that keeps the brief, decisions, branch and SHA). That costs about 5 minutes.
> The noVNC keyboard-layout bug did not go to `rdp-audio`. It is a new task, T<n>, status `brainstorm`, and both product advisors are drafting its design (round 1 of 3).
> **Next.** `rdp-audio`: compact, confirm branch and SHA, then tasks 8–9, cross-model review, my validation, and your final-PR poll. T<n>: critique, merge, 2/2 design approval, then a fresh executor tab in its own worktree.
> **From you.** Nothing. Stage 0 runs for T<n> under your ruling "every task is brainstormed" unless you waive it.
> Vote decisions since the last status: none. Backlog: <Artifact URL>

**7. When the waiter from step 3 fires.** I read `<inbox>/rdp-audio.last`, then run `herdr agent get rdp-audio`. I check the reported SHA myself with `git -C ~/work/ccs.ansible/.claude/worktrees/rdp-audio log -1 --format=%H` and `status --short`. Then, Bash, background:
```bash
herdr agent prompt rdp-audio "/compact mid-task: keep the brief, the decisions, DIR/branch/head SHA and the open items" --wait --timeout 300000; \
herdr agent read rdp-audio --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > <inbox>/rdp-audio.last
```
Next, in background, the message `One-line status: phase, branch, head SHA, next step. Reply in English.`, which I check against git. Last, in background with the brief's time box:
`Continue with tasks 8 and 9 of the plan under superpowers:test-driven-development; before reporting done use superpowers:verification-before-completion. Scope unchanged. REPORT as in your brief. Reply in English.`

## Why

- **The noVNC bug is new work.** It raises a design question the rdp-audio design doc does not answer, so it enters the backlog at `brainstorm` and gets its own tab and worktree (§4, §10a). A second task in the same tab inherits the first one's assumptions and a context that is already 70% full.
- **The rules I am following are the operator's own standing rulings.** "Every task is brainstormed" and "one worktree per task" (§15) outrank a chat request. Only the operator's waiver removes stage 0, and I neither assume it nor design the fix myself.
- **"Don't interrupt" is honoured in substance.** I send no `esc`, and the running step finishes and commits. Compaction is still due: 70% is past the threshold, and tasks 8–9 plus verification would otherwise hit auto-compaction mid-step, which keeps the wrong things. A tab working through a plan never goes idle between steps, so the queued message is the only safe point (§4).
- **Everything waits in the background.** A foreground wait would leave nobody supervising the other tabs (§3).
- **The status says "still running".** A working tab has no result to report (§12).
- **No poll.** Nothing here is one of the operator's four decisions, and no deadline forces a choice between slipping and waiving.
